 @baraadw6959  To add on with what you were saying:

3050 is handicapped by only being wired up with 8 lanes of PCIE express. Not a problem on MBs that have PCIE 4.0. 1660 Super has the full-fat 16x, so it can function on a 3.0 slot just fine. To put it in other words, you could have potentially used a card like the 1660S to upgrade a entry level office PC (most go for 1650 because no PSU pcie cable required, but whatever) could function fine on a 2.0 slot. Considering other bottlenecks a system limited to an anemic 2.0 pcie bus would also carry with it (Intel 2nd/3rd generation etc.)

This is now the same problem gamers will face when using a 3050 on most MBs released pre-2020. Handicapped maximum GPU speed.

